# github — the GitHub flow: the workflow stubs in .github/workflows/, the repo's
# branch rules (rulesets) and the release model (merge to main = release
# candidate, CalVer tag = promote). Enabling the plugin means letting the rig
# own .github/. The site writes no workflows of its own. That is what the level
# `delivery` means, and LEVEL below is what the runner derives the level from.
# RIG_GITHUB_SKIP opts out of stubs by name (without .yml), e.g. main when
# the site should not deploy to dev yet; a rig-owned one of those is cleaned up.
# The build contract (ci) follows the stack; REQUIRES exists because the stubs
# call ci-* and are meaningless without it. Vendoring lives in vendor.sh.
NAME=github
KIND=addon
REQUIRES=ci
LEVEL=delivery
KEYS=RIG_GITHUB_SKIP
